#X text 240 83 MQTT (Message Queuing Telemetry Transport) is a lightweight
publish/subscribe messaging protocol designed for constrained devices
and low-bandwidth networks;
#X text 240 138 the object connects to an MQTT broker \, publishes
messages to topics and subscribes to receive messages from them;
#X text 240 193 @qos sets the quality of service level (0 — at most
once \, 1 — at least once \, 2 — exactly once);
#X text 240 233 the second outlet outputs a bang when a ping message
is received from the broker;
#X text 50 336 you can start testing mqtt server with command: 'nanomq
-start';
